---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Contact" ogTitle="Contact" ogDescription="Get in touch with questions or suggestions.">
  <h1>Contact</h1>

  <p>
    For anything at all — questions, suggestions, feedback, or adding a book to the
    library — please write to Michael Coughlin:
  </p>
  <p class="fs-5 mb-4">
    <a class="js-email" data-u="enonaereba" data-d="em.mp" href="/contact/">Email Michael</a>
  </p>

  <p class="text-body-secondary">
    Only if that fails — no reply after a while, or the mail bounces — try Courtney Hicks
    at <a class="js-email" data-u="yleerf.skoob" data-d="moc.xendnyl" href="/contact/">Courtney's email</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Add a Resource</h2>
  <p>
    Would you like to add a book to the library? You can submit a resource under a freely given,
    public domain license by visiting
    <a href="https://freely.giving/publish?type=books">freely.giving/publish</a> to see what you
    need to do, then email Michael at the address above.
  </p>
  <noscript><p class="text-body-secondary">The email addresses on this page need JavaScript turned on.</p></noscript>
  <script is:inline>
    // Addresses are stored reversed and split so scrapers reading the raw HTML don't find them;
    // they're put back together in the browser.
    document.querySelectorAll('.js-email').forEach(function (a) {
      var rev = function (s) { return s.split('').reverse().join(''); };
      var addr = rev(a.dataset.u) + '@' + rev(a.dataset.d);
      a.href = 'mailto:' + addr;
      a.textContent = addr;
    });
  </script>
</Base>
